## 2. Wire it into the endpoint securely

```python
import logging
import uuid

logger = logging.getLogger("math.eval")

@app.post("/evaluate")
async def evaluate_endpoint(payload: ExpressionIn, user=Depends(current_user)):
    request_id = str(uuid.uuid4())
    try:
        result = evaluator.evaluate(payload.expression)
    except UnsafeExpression as exc:
        logger.warning(
            "expression_rejected request_id=%s user_id=%s reason=%s len=%d",
            request_id, user.id, exc, len(payload.expression),
        )
        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="Invalid expression")  # generic
    logger.info("expression_ok request_id=%s user_id=%s", request_id, user.id)
    return {"result": result}
```

The four things that matter here, mapped to the OWASP findings the hardening builder returned:

| Control | Why | OWASP |
|---|---|---|
| AST allowlist instead of `eval` | Removes the injection class entirely | **A03 Injection** |
| Deny-by-default node set + size/depth/exponent caps | Secure design, not bolted-on filtering | **A04 Insecure Design** |
| Generic client error, full
